{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016TNPQHffG6noZioNCjgEyw","type":"tool_result","content":"# SPDX Definition and SBOM Information\n\n**What SPDX is:**\n\"The System Package Data Exchange (SPDX®) specification is an open standard designed to facilitate the communication of Bill of Materials (BOM) information across diverse domains, including software, artificial intelligence (AI), datasets, and system components.\"\n\n**Definition of SBOM:**\nNOT ON PAGE (The page uses \"Bill of Materials\" or \"BOM\" but does not provide a standalone definition of \"SBOM\")\n\n**What an SBOM contains:**\nThe page addresses components through SPDX's coverage: \"Metadata for collections of software (Packages), individual Files, and portions of files (Snippets)\" plus \"Comprehensive licensing information\" and \"Provenance and Integrity: Tracking the origin and history of components, including checksums and cryptographic hashes.\"\n\n**Why SBOMs matter for supply chain security:**\nNOT ON PAGE (The page does not explicitly connect SBOMs to vulnerability management or supply chain security risks)\n\n**SPDX organizational details:**\n\"SPDX is a collaborative effort driven by the Linux Foundation and supported by a global community of developers, organizations, and industry experts.\"\n\n\"SPDX 3.0 (a major revision to SPDX 2.2.1, aka free ISO/IEC 5962:2021 – SPDX® Specification V2.2.1)\""}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bf938bdb-ceb6-4379-83e1-38e2e5739719","uuid":"c5b2f134-c912-4e20-98c3-4e7b8db9a95a","timestamp":"2026-08-31T04:28:38.501Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":30984,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# SPDX Definition and SBOM Information\n\n**What SPDX is:**\n\"The System Package Data Exchange (SPDX®) specification is an open standard designed to facilitate the communication of Bill of Materials (BOM) information across diverse domains, including software, artificial intelligence (AI), datasets, and system components.\"\n\n**Definition of SBOM:**\nNOT ON PAGE (The page uses \"Bill of Materials\" or \"BOM\" but does not provide a standalone definition of \"SBOM\")\n\n**What an SBOM contains:**\nThe page addresses components through SPDX's coverage: \"Metadata for collections of software (Packages), individual Files, and portions of files (Snippets)\" plus \"Comprehensive licensing information\" and \"Provenance and Integrity: Tracking the origin and history of components, including checksums and cryptographic hashes.\"\n\n**Why SBOMs matter for supply chain security:**\nNOT ON PAGE (The page does not explicitly connect SBOMs to vulnerability management or supply chain security risks)\n\n**SPDX organizational details:**\n\"SPDX is a collaborative effort driven by the Linux Foundation and supported by a global community of developers, organizations, and industry experts.\"\n\n\"SPDX 3.0 (a major revision to SPDX 2.2.1, aka free ISO/IEC 5962:2021 – SPDX® Specification V2.2.1)\"","durationMs":20435,"url":"https://spdx.dev/learn/overview/"}}
